      "description": "Explicit fixture provenance with an amber dot; never a live-success badge.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-tag\" title=\"Fixture data. Nothing here was observed on a network.\"><span class=\"ds-dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Simulated</span>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;min-height:26px;padding:0 10px;border-radius:999px;background:#fbf3e4;color:var(--sim);font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.55;white-space:normal;}.ds-dot{width:8px;height:8px;flex:none;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sim-dot);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "White evidence surface; this static sample keeps its state explicitly untested.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-card\"><h3 class=\"ds-card-title\">Worker</h3><p class=\"ds-card-lead\">Not started</p><p class=\"ds-card-sub\">Untested. Run a step to collect evidence.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-card{min-width:0;padding:24px;border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card);font-family:var(--font-text);line-height:1.55;}.ds-card-title{margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;}.ds-card-lead{margin:0;color:var(--ink-3);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.02em;}.ds-card-sub{margin:4px 0 0;color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.9375rem;}@media(max-width:520px){.ds-card{padding:20px;}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Private-mode Switch",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "switch",
      "description": "The current on-state sample uses aria-checked and the real extended hit area.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-switch\" role=\"switch\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Private mode\"><span class=\"ds-thumb\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></button>",
      "css": ".ds-switch{position:relative;width:44px;height:26px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:var(--line-strong);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .25s var(--ease-out);}.ds-switch:before{content:\"\";position:absolute;inset:-9px 0;}.ds-thumb{position:absolute;top:3px;left:3px;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgb(23 20 31 / .25);transition:transform .3s var(--ease-out);}.ds-switch[aria-checked=\"true\"]{background:var(--protected);}.ds-switch[aria-checked=\"true\"] .ds-thumb{transform:translateX(18px);}.ds-switch:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--protected);outline-offset:3px;}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-primary,.ds-secondary,.ds-nav a,.ds-switch,.ds-thumb,.ds-step{transition-duration:0.01ms!important;animation-duration:0.01ms!important;animation-iteration-count:1!important;}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Current Guide Step",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "guide-step-current",
      "description": "A current step uses white fill and a dark marker; the sample does not execute a lab action.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-step\" aria-current=\"step\"><span class=\"ds-step-marker\">1</span>Read privately</button>",
      "css": ".ds-step{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;width:100%;min-height:48px;padding:8px 12px;border:0;border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:none;color:var(--ink-2);font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.55;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .2s;}.ds-step:hover{background:rgb(255 255 255 / .6);}.ds-step[aria-current=\"step\"]{background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;box-shadow:var(--shadow-float);}.ds-step-marker{display:grid;place-items:center;width:26px;height:26px;flex:none;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink);color:#fff;font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:600;}.ds-step:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--protected);outline-offset:3px;}@media(max-width:899px){.ds-step{align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;height:100%;font-size:.875rem;}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-primary,.ds-secondary,.ds-nav a,.ds-switch,.ds-thumb,.ds-step{transition-duration:0.01ms!important;animation-duration:0.01ms!important;animation-iteration-count:1!important;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Guided Lab",
    "overview": "The light guided surface preserves the owner's requested Phantom-inspired direction: a lavender-grey page, white cards, a restrained purple action, and an original dark route stage. Dark ink and readable labels keep the surrounding interface clear in a lit room; the contained stage carries the expressive geometry. The Monolith mark and route model remain original.\n\nThe visual system makes the next action easy to find and keeps results, residual exposure and provenance readable together. [PRODUCT.md](PRODUCT.md) carries product truth; [the guided-lab brief](.impeccable/guided-lab.md) carries this surface's mode and composition. This document merges the established MN-006 shell guidance with the implemented refinement, extracting values from [tokens.css](src/styles/tokens.css), [lab.css](src/styles/lab.css) and the existing components. The frontmatter records implemented primitives; it does not add CSS variables. Sidecar tonal ramps are derived preview swatches, not additional application tokens.\n\nThe default app is now the live composition; `?mode=simulated` opens the separate offline fixture walkthrough. The persistent mode badge names the selected mode, while result badges establish a run's provenance. The original [MN-006 review](docs/review/README.md) remains historical SIMULATED shell evidence. Its desktop, 390px, 320px and WebGL-fallback screenshots, and screenshots made for this refinement, establish presentation behavior only; they provide no new live anonymity, registry, payment or sponsor evidence.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale lavender ground with dark readable ink and white result surfaces.",
      "Purple actions and protected-route labels; red exposure and amber simulation labels.",
      "A contained dark route stage with a readable text counterpart.",
      "Self-hosted typography, visible keyboard focus and reduced-motion support."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Use purple for the primary action and protected route, red for direct exposure, green for a passing check, and amber for simulated data. A color or animation never grants evidence credit.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the lavender ground, white working surfaces and contained original dark route stage.",
      "**Do** keep the next primary action visible and give secondary evidence a readable hierarchy.",
      "**Do** pair meaning colors with text or icons and preserve explicit mode and result provenance.",
      "**Do** retain self-hosted fonts, keyboard focus, reduced motion and the SVG/text fallback.",
      "**Do** show both route protection and the payload information the endpoint can still read."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** treat a live-mode label, route animation or presentation screenshot as observed anonymity evidence.",
      "**Don't** turn unavailable or unmeasured results into green success, full coverage or a fabricated score.",
      "**Don't** hide a direct bypass when a managed read fails closed during an outage.",
      "**Don't** depict payment as anonymous or activate it from visual styling alone.",
      "**Don't** copy another product's mascot, mark or visual assets into the original Monolith stage."
    ]
  }
}
